    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T17:05:34Z",
    "body": "Research note from #308 (multi-setup carried stock), code on `main` 2026-11-08:\n\n- **Why no setup can pick an offset today:** the slot is not stored on the setup at all. `posting::wcs_context` infers it **per operation** from the first height that references a work offset (`HeightReference::WorkOffset(i)`), defaulting to G54; generation (`operation/job.rs`), the stamp, the spindle law and the machine travel check all call that same function. The fix is a slot on `SetupDef` (undoable, saved) that `wcs_context` reads first, with the per-op height reference kept as an explicit override - one law, so every caller follows.\n- **Related P0 found on the way:** the offset's **rotation** is dropped when posting (only `OriginX/Y/Z` reach the post) - filed as #315. A per-setup offset that comes from a 3-2-1 alignment will hit it, so #315's refusal should land first.\n- This issue is now the work-offset prerequisite of #316 (setup-to-setup transform), part of #308.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
